# Atlas Security Rules

Canonical decision: `docs/architecture/adr-001-acting-first-eve.md`.

- Never commit secrets.
- Encrypt OAuth refresh tokens.
- Use least-privilege scopes.
- Do not log secrets or sensitive raw content.
- MVP is single-user (R0). When sharing ships, enforce visibility server-side.
- Connector secrets and OAuth tokens never go to models or channel adapters as raw values.
- Destructive external actions are forbidden in MVP.
- Real external writes require short confirmation (P1); drafts and internal safe writes may auto-run.
- Do not request or share personal provider account passwords, 2FA, or broad production dashboard access.
- Provider/env changes must update `.env.example`, provider docs, and doctor/env checks.
- Do not store raw payment credentials or card data in Atlas Postgres.
- Live payment enablement needs PCI-boundary review, webhook verification, rollback, and explicit approval.
- Use deterministic purpose-bound disclosure from `docs/architecture/privacy-redaction-policy.md`.
- Secrets, OAuth tokens, refresh tokens, passwords, private keys, session material, raw card data, and CVV must never be sent to LLMs.
- Real user-derived fixtures must be redacted before commit unless Efe approves an encrypted local-only development bundle.
